## How the plugin's commands consume Entry

- `/bcq-review` runs the `al-entry` skill. Entry routes a broad goal to `al-code-review`, which runs its 19 leaves and the self-review.
- `/bcq-review-<domain>` runs `al-entry` with a goal naming that domain, so Entry selects the leaf (`narrower-sub-skill-selected`). `/bcq-review-agents` selects the community peer, which `/bcq-review` never runs.
- `al-entry` never dispatches Entry recursively.

## When to load this file

- Before invoking `al-entry` to route a task.
- When debugging why a leaf was or was not dispatched.
- Before adding a custom action skill under `content/bcquality/custom/skills/`. Use the same `id` as an upstream skill to override it, or a new `id` to add a skill. Update `al-entry`'s candidate list too.
